<title>JAPAN: Takefuji ask-only after secondary share offer news.</title>
<headline>Takefuji ask-only after secondary share offer news.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Takefuji Corp shares were ask-only in early Tuesday morning trade after the personal loan firm announced that it was planning to make a secondary offering of three million shares, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0030 GMT, the shares were ask-only at 7,880 yen in over-the-counter trade, after closing at 7,980 yen in the Monday session.  </p>
<p>On Monday, Takefuji said in a statement that two Tokyo-based companies which hold Takefuji shares will sell a total of three million shares.</p>
<p>Of the three million shares, one million will be sold in Japan and the rest will be sold overseas, it said.</p>
